{"fields":{"advisory":{"aliases":[],"categories":["memory-exposure","memory-corruption"],"collection":"crates","cvss":null,"date":"2026-10-16","description":"`ZSTD_seekable_decompress` shortens the requested length to the end of the\r\ndata without checking that the offset is before it. For an offset past the\r\nend, it returns a wrapped-around length without writing anything, and\r\n`Seekable::decompress` passed that length to `Vec::set_len`.\r\n\r\nWith the `seekable` feature, whoever supplies the archive, or chooses the\r\noffset, can leave the caller's `Vec<u8>` with a length far beyond its\r\ncapacity. Reading it then discloses neighbouring heap memory, and appending\r\nto it corrupts memory. Offsets near `u64::MAX` can also hang the call.\r\n\r\nThe flaw was corrected by clamping requests to the end of the data, and by\r\nchecking every count reported by the C library against the buffer capacity.","expect-deleted":false,"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0398","informational":null,"keywords":["seekable","out-of-bounds"],"license":"CC0-1.0","package":"zstd-safe","references":["https://github.com/gyscos/zstd-rs/pull/384"],"related":[],"source":null,"title":"`Seekable::decompress` sets a `Vec` length beyond its capacity for offsets past the end","url":"https://github.com/gyscos/zstd-rs/commit/80506be743fae2ed0c2fe8b21c374c6a2eab0be7","withdrawn":null},"code":"vulnerability","graphs":[{"Krate":{"name":"zstd-safe","version":"7.2.4"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"zstd","version":"0.13.3"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"chitchat","version":"0.11.1"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"hydracache-cluster-chitchat","version":"0.73.0"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"hydracache-cluster","version":"0.73.0"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"kind":"dev","name":"hydracache-post-publish-consumer","version":"0.73.0"}}]},{"Krate":{"kind":"dev","name":"hydracache-cluster-raft","version":"0.73.0"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"hydracache-cluster","version":"0.73.0"},"repeat":true},{"Krate":{"name":"hydracache-cluster-t